  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\n\nThe center of a large mid level ridge remains over the TN Valley\ntoday. ILN/s area is in the warm and moist airmass with PWAT \nvalues around 2 inches. Surface dewpoints in the lower and middle 70s\nand highs from the mid 80s north to the lower 90s south. This will \nresult in maximum heat indices of 95 to around 100 across the south. \n\nMorning convection has shifted east of the area and weakened. Focus \nshifts to MCV which tracks east in the westerly flow around the\nperiphery of the ridge across central and northern Ohio. This \ncombined with moderate instability will lead to scattered storms late\nthis afternoon into early evening. The best coverage of storms looks\nto impact areas along and north of I-70. DCAPE values approaching \n1000 J/KG suggest that a few for the stronger storms could produce \nstrong to damaging winds but an organized threat appears unlikely. \nThe greater threat will likely be for heavy rain, with PWAT values \naround 2 inches. Also, model solutions suggest that a 8H low level \njet around 30 kts will act to generate a potential MCS. This complex \nwill likely develop into west central Ohio late tonight and move thru\nthe area Thursday morning. The exact placement of this feature is \nsomewhat uncertain but the most likely location is along and north of\nthe I-70 corridor. HREF LPMM suggest that the potential exists for \nswaths of 2 to 4 inches with locally up to 5 inches thru Thursday. \nThis area has received heavy rain last night. This lines up with WPC\nforecast area in slight risk of excessive rainfall today and \nmarginal risk on Thursday. Will issue a flood watch for potential \nflash flooding overnight into Thursday. \n\nThe northern portion of the mid level ridge breaks down as the center\nof the high retrogrades west across the Lower MS Valley into the \nSouthern Plains on Friday. This will allow the surface front to shift\nsouth into the Ohio Valley, lowering max temps, but increasing \nprecipitation chances across the south prior to ending. A brief \nrespite in rain will exist later Friday into early Saturday with \nadditional rain expected Saturday night and Sunday. Forecast \nconfidence becomes lower in any specifics this weekend.",
